<title>THAILAND: National Fertilizer to sign $34 mln loan package.</title>
<headline>National Fertilizer to sign $34 mln loan package.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand National Fertilizer Plc will sign a loan package worth $34 million on Friday, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Industrial Finance Corporation of Thailand Plc, Krung Thai Bank Plc, Siam City Bank Plc and Siam Commercial Bank Plc are the lenders, the statement said.</p>
<p>The loans consist of an $11.4 million tranche carrying an interest rate of 250 basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate (LIBOR) and a 676 million baht ($22.5 million) tranche at a rate of 100 basis points over LIBOR. The tenors are 10 years.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be spent on constructing a sulphuric-acid plant, the firm said.</p>
<p>($1 = 30 baht)</p>
</text>
